-- title:
--   Any mod-p retraction of ι₀ reads q-expansions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \ge 1$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that maps to $1$ under $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Assume the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` $= q^{-1}\cdot(\text{integral power series } E_4^3\eta^{-24})$ lies in $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of level one. For a group $\Gamma$, write $\mathcal{O}_\Gamma$ for the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}[j_\Gamma]$ inside the corresponding $q$-expansion function field $\mathrm{qExpFunctionFieldC}\,\mathbb{Q}\,\Gamma \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, and put $\mathcal{O}_N = \mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_N}$, $\mathcal{O}_M = \mathcal{O}_{\Gamma_M}$ for the groups `ΓN p M H hpM` and `ΓM M H`. Given a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra map $\iota_0 : \mathcal{O}_N \to \mathcal{O}_M$ preserving $q$-expansions, a $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$-algebra automorphism $\theta$ of $\mathcal{O}_M$ with $\theta(\iota_0 b)$ having $q$-expansion $b(q^p)$ (the exponent-scaling map `qExpand ℚ p`), an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $p$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, and any $\kappa$-algebra map $\sigma_0 : \kappa \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}} \mathcal{O}_M \to \kappa \otimes \mathcal{O}_N$ retracting $\mathrm{id} \otimes \iota_0$, there exist a ring homomorphism $\Theta : \mathcal{O}_M \to \kappa((q))$ and an injective $\kappa$-algebra map $e : \kappa \otimes \mathcal{O}_N \to \kappa((q))$ such that $e(\sigma_0(a \otimes c)) = a\,\Theta(c)$ for all $a \in \kappa$, $c \in \mathcal{O}_M$, and such that whenever the $q$-expansion of $c$ is the image of a Laurent series $y$ over $\mathbb{Z}$, one has $\Theta(c) =$ the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ to $\kappa((q))$.
--
--   This identifies every $\kappa$-algebra retraction of $\kappa \otimes \iota_0$, up to the embedding $e$, with the reduction mod $p$ of the $q$-expansion reading on the first copy of the $\Gamma_H(M)$-chart, the case $p \parallel M$ of the Deligne–Rapoport description of the fibre at $p$ of the modular curve. It feeds the computations of which elements are killed by the reduction of $\theta$ in [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.exists_retraction_tmul_theta_eq_zero_and_mem_iff_exists_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.exists_retraction_tmul_theta_eq_zero_and_mem_iff_exists_mem_ssJSet) and [`ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.retraction_map_theta_eq_zero_mem_of_mem_ssJSet_gammaH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRLevel.retraction_map_theta_eq_zero_mem_of_mem_ssJSet_gammaH).
